n. The table shows for\n967:results (column Exact). All percentages of Table 1 relate to column Loops.\n973:    The last column of Table 1 shows the percentage of loops for which exact iteration\n978:analysis of pointers which can not always be precisely evaluated in a static analysis.\n984:Table 1 Precision of loop analysis\n995:272                                                        Real-Time Syst (2010) 46: 251–300\n997:Table 2 Run times of loop analysis\n1010:via the innovative polytope-based loop evaluation, which shows that the prerequisites\n1011:of this polyhedral evaluation are not too restrictive and are often met in real-life code.\n1012:5.5.2 Analysis time\n1016:polyhedral loop evaluation can not be applied, the analysis based on abstract interpre-\n1021:benchmarks is shown in Table 2. Column Basic represents the absolute run time of\n1025:evaluation (including slicing). In addition, values in parentheses found in the fourth\n1027:    Table 2 shows that slicing significantly decreases analysis times. For matmul, a\n1028:reduction of 72% was achieved. matmul also benefits from the polytope approach. It\n1029:contains some loops that can be statically evaluated using the polyhedral model that\n1030:leads to a further reduction in time of 27%. For other benchmarks like mult_10_10,\n1034:evaluation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
